      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 52-year-old man presented to the emergency department with a one-day history of epigastric pain. The patient reported a remote history of a \"difficult\" laparoscopic cholecystectomy that was converted to an open cholecystectomy in 1994. Further operative details were unavailable. Multiple radiologic studies were obtained, all demonstrating a saccular cystic structure in the gallbladder fossa containing calculi. A completion open cholecystectomy, or \"recholecystectomy,\" revealed a remnant gallbladder with cholecystitis and cholelithiasis. Multimodality imaging findings are reviewed."},
